<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian three-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 9.987 percent from 9.999 percent at the previous auction on February 19.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: May 29, 1997 (May 22, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.987 percent (9.999)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 986.125 million (980.775 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,079.125 million (1,055.825 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 9.800-10.061 percent (9.800-10.091)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 9.800-10.133 percent (9.800-11.300)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 128 (127)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 147 (135)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
